16J. (1) Subject to sub-regulation (2), the following communications shall not be considered as
'advertisement':
(a) communication that is educational or informational in nature and is meant to impart
financial knowledge or information or training. For such communication, the regulated
entity shall comply with the following:
(i) branding of the entity in such communications shall be minimal and incidental;
(ii) such communication shall not contain any promotional call-to-action or attempt to
influence or induce a purchase decision for a specific product or service provided by the
regulated entity;
(iii) if the cost towards such communication is being borne out of funds earmarked for
education and awareness, such communications shall be reported to the supervisory body
or Board for post facto monitoring;
(b) research reports or recommendations or analyses shared with existing clients or
investors which do not contain claims of performance of the regulated entity;
(c) list of available products or services, including lists provided on regulated entity's
website or app, which provides a summary of factual information about the products or
services of the regulated entity;
(d) essential communication between regulated entities and existing clients or investors
arising out of any regulatory requirement;
(e) communication in response to a request by a client or prospective client or investor
for information about any product or service;
(f) communication providing basic factual information about regulated entity (such as
name, brand logo, website or app or similar details) and a description of the nature of its

activities;
(g) product demonstrations (e.g. webinars, walk-throughs) showing the interface and
service features provided such demonstration does not promote products or services or
solicit interest to avail any product or service of the regulated entity;
(h) greetings, condolences or congratulatory messages;
(i) public communications inviting applications for recruitment or availing third party
services provided it does not target clients or prospective clients or investors;
(j) sponsorship for TV shows or talk shows and events communicating generic
information about the regulated entity such as name, brand name, logo, website or app or
similar details and is only limited to sponsorship;
(k) surveys issued by the regulated entities to their registered clients or investors to take
feedback; and
(l) any other communication as may be specified by the Board from time to time.
(2) Any communication which promotes products or services or solicits interest to avail
any product or service of a regulated entity shall be considered as an advertisement.
Celebrity Endorsements

16L. (1) The regulated entity shall ensure compliance with the following:
(a) advertisements shall be true, fair, accurate, complete and unambiguous;
(b) advertisements shall not be so designed as likely to be misunderstood or likely to
disguise the significance of any statement;
(c) advertisements shall not be so framed as to exploit the lack of experience or
knowledge of the investors;
(d) advertisements shall not extensively use technical or legal terminology or complex
language or include excessive details, which may mislead or confuse the investors;
(e) a disclaimer stating that “The securities or scheme(s) are quoted as an example and
not as a recommendation” shall be mentioned on the same page of the written creative or
frame of the video where the same is displayed and not at the end of the creative or the
advertisement, in case any specific securities or scheme(s) are displayed or
communicated in an advertisement as example(s);
(f) disclosures in the terms of statistical data, graphs, or charts shall be backed by
source(s) and the source(s) shall be disclosed alongside such data, graphs, or charts.
Further, such statistical data, graphs, or charts shall include the date or period to which it
relates;
(g) regulated entities shall refrain from providing any form of incentives, or vouchers, or
coupons, or monetary certificates, or tokens, or subscription plans, by whatever name
called, to their clients for inducement to trade or avail the services or for activation of
inactive client accounts or investing into any schemes or for downloading mobile
applications etc.;
