16O. An advertisement shall not contain:
(a) any content, which is false, misleading, luring, biased, deceptive, exaggerated,
ambiguous or based on assumptions or projections or includes any testimonials;
(b) anything that, directly or indirectly, promises or gives assurance of any guaranteed or
risk free or indicative returns to prospective or existing clients;
(c) any direct or indirect promise or assurance of any fixed returns (except in case of
Online Bond Platform Providers or any other entity in a form and manner as may be
specified by the Board);
(d) any content that, directly or indirectly, disparages or discredits other regulated
entities, their products or services or makes unfair comparisons with such entities or
imitates the advertisement content of other regulated entities;
(e) any content that compares one product or asset class with other product(s) or asset
class(es) of a different nature giving a misleading impression;
(f) any content designed to exploit the lack of experience or knowledge of the investors
or any slogan that is exaggerated or unwarranted or inconsistent with or unrelated to the
nature and risk and return profile of the products or services being advertised;
(g) logos, images (e.g. building imagery) or symbols of the Board or Market
Infrastructure Institutions (MIIs) or any other organisation of such repute, unless
specifically permitted;
(h) any content that implies that past performance may recur or makes any unwarranted
claim;
(i) any reference to past performance in respect of the products or services of regulated
entities unless the past performance is communicated in the manner as specified by

Board from time to time;
(j) any content which is indecent, vulgar or offensive;
(k) adjectives such as high yield, high rated, high returns and synonyms of such words,
which are vague and general without any basis;
(l) anything, which is prohibited for publication or communication under the law;
(m) any other communication as may be specified by the Board or supervisory body in
consultation with the Board, from time to time.
